    <!-- Main Content Overlapping Hero -->
    <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full px-6 py-8 -mt-16 relative z-20 macos-glass mb-12">
        
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><span class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/10 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1"><svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg> 4 MIN READ</span></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10 pb-6">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">Growth</h2>
            <div class="w-24 h-1 rounded-full opacity-80" style="background-color: #84cc16"></div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="prose  max-w-none">
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Spiritual Disciplines</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Growth doesn't happen by accident — it never has and it never will. It happens through intentional, daily practices that position your heart before God: Bible reading, prayer, fasting, worship, journaling, and silence. Paul told Timothy plainly in 1 Timothy 4:7, "Train yourself in godliness." That word "train" is the Greek word "gymnazo" — it's where we get the word gymnasium.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Spiritual growth requires the same kind of discipline an athlete brings to their sport: showing up when you don't feel like it, pushing through when it's uncomfortable, and trusting the process when you can't see results yet. But hear this clearly — these disciplines are not religious rules designed to earn God's approval. You already have His approval through the cross.</p><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">These are relational rhythms, sacred habits that keep you connected to the Vine so that you can bear fruit (John 15:4-5). They're less like a checklist and more like breathing — essential, life-giving, and deeply personal.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>The Word of God</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">2 Timothy 3:16-17 declares that all Scripture is God-breathed and useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting, and training in righteousness — so that the servant of God may be thoroughly equipped for every good work. The Bible is not a dusty textbook or a collection of ancient rules. It is a living, active, and sharp word from the Creator of the universe directly to you (Hebrews 4:12).</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Learn to read it not as an obligation but as a love letter — because that's exactly what it is. God is speaking to you through every page, every story, every promise. If you don't know where to start, begin with the Gospels — Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John — and watch Jesus walk, teach, heal, and love in real time.</p><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Use a reading plan to give you structure so you don't get lost or overwhelmed. Journal what the Holy Spirit highlights to you, because He will highlight something — He promised He would guide you into all truth (John 16:13). The Word of God isn't just information; it's formation.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">It shapes who you're becoming.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Prayer &amp; Fasting</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Prayer is not a monologue — it's a conversation with the living God who knows your name and counts the hairs on your head. It's honest, raw, unfiltered communion where you bring everything — your fears, your doubts, your gratitude, your confusion — and lay it at the feet of a Father who actually listens. And fasting? Fasting is saying with your body what your mouth can't always express: "God, I want You more than food, more than comfort, more than control, more than the next dopamine hit from my phone." Jesus assumed His followers would fast — not "if" you fast, but "when" you fast (Matthew 6:16-18).</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Fasting sharpens your spiritual hearing, breaks strongholds, and realigns your appetites with the kingdom. As a ministry, we practice corporate fasting seasons together — because there's something powerful about an entire community saying "no" to the flesh and "yes" to the Spirit at the same time. We've seen God move in extraordinary ways during these seasons: breakthroughs in mental health, clarity on calling, and restored relationships.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>The Role of the Holy Spirit</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Here's a truth that will save you from exhaustion: you cannot grow by self-effort. If you could, you wouldn't need a Savior. Galatians 5:16 says, "Walk by the Spirit, and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh." The Christian life was never designed to be powered by willpower — it's powered by the Holy Spirit living inside you.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">He is your teacher who brings Scripture to life and reminds you of everything Jesus said (John 14:26). He is your comforter who meets you in your grief, your loneliness, and your darkest nights. He is your power source who gives you the strength to forgive when it feels impossible, to love when you've been hurt, and to keep going when everything in you wants to quit.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">The invitation is simple but transformative: invite the Holy Spirit into every area of your life — your relationships, your finances, your career decisions, your thought life, your social media habits, all of it. Stop trying to manage your life and start surrendering it. He's not a guest in your house; He's the rightful owner.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Let Him lead, and watch the fruit grow.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10">
